<title>MEXICO: Mexico considers 500 bln lira debt issue - report.</title>
<headline>Mexico considers 500 bln lira debt issue - report.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico is considering a 500 billion Italian lira debt issue on international markets, Reforma newspaper reported Wednesday, quoting market sources in New York.</p>
<p>Reforma said the issue of floating-rate notes would have a maturity of five years.</p>
<p>It gave no other details.</p>
<p>Officials at the finance ministry were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>--Martin Langfield, Mexico City newsroom 525 7289558</p>
